# Generated files.
#
# These are committed on purpose: `pkg/pluginsdk` is a public Go module surface
# (a `go get` of the plugin SDK compiles what the module ships, it never runs
# protoc), the templ output is what makes `go build ./...` work without a
# toolchain, and `assets/` is consumed through //go:embed.
#
# `linguist-generated` collapses them by default in GitHub diffs and keeps them
# out of the language statistics. `-diff` does the same locally.
#
# `merge=ours` needs a one-off local opt-in, otherwise git warns and falls back
# to the default driver:
#
#     git config merge.ours.driver true
#
# The right fix for a conflict on a generated file is to re-run `make generate`
# anyway, so keeping "ours" and regenerating loses nothing.

*_templ.go                 linguist-generated=true -diff merge=ours
*.pb.go                    linguist-generated=true -diff merge=ours
internal/http/handler/webui/common/assets/templui.css        linguist-generated=true -diff merge=ours
internal/http/handler/webui/pipeline/assets/dist/**          linguist-generated=true -diff merge=ours

# Vendored third-party assets: not ours, no point diffing them either.
internal/http/handler/webui/common/assets/js/*.min.js        linguist-vendored=true -diff
internal/http/handler/webui/common/assets/*.min.js           linguist-vendored=true -diff
internal/http/handler/webui/common/assets/vendor/**          linguist-vendored=true -diff
